# Real-time Candle Visualization System (Phase 1: Mocking)

## Core Architecture

- Next.js App Router only.
- Lightweight Charts for rendering.
- GBM-based mock tick generation.
- Tick → 1m OHLC aggregation.
- High-frequency ticks buffered in queue/ref, NEVER in React state or Zustand.
- Queue consumption ONLY inside requestAnimationFrame.
- Pause producer/consumer when tab is hidden (visibilitychange).

## SSR Safety

- Chart components: dynamic import with ssr: false.
- Any window/document usage: client-only components.
- Server components for layout/UI only.

## Performance Rules

- Minimize React re-renders.
- useRef for chart instance, series, queue, live candle.
- Batch queue consumption per RAF frame.
- No setInterval/setTimeout for rendering.
- Background tab: pause everything.

## Data Flow

1. GBM Producer → Tick {ts: unix ms, price: number} to queue
2. RAF Consumer → drain queue → aggregate to OHLC
3. Lightweight Charts series.update() for live candle
4. New minute → new candle

## Coding Style

- TypeScript strict.
- Small focused files.
- Pure functions for GBM/aggregate.
- Comments only for non-obvious logic.
- Minimal diffs.

## Output Format

When implementing:

1. Code changes
2. What it does
3. Why this approach
4. Any assumptions
5. Next logical step
